WEBVTT

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:02.800
Why DCC MCP, when AI can write code?

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.933
Creative teams need workflows

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.233
they can reuse and manage.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.900
Skills explain how a task works.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.267
MCP connects the assistant to software tools.

00:00:13.967 --> 00:00:16.167
DCC MCP brings them together.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:17.833
Discover relevant tools

00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:19.100
and load their instructions.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:22.300
Reusable skills reduce repeated code generation

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.967
and unnecessary token usage.

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:26.467
Rust handles key routing in compiled code,

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.233
reducing interpreter overhead.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.133
Python remains available for host scripts.

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:34.200
Permission policies define execution boundaries.

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:36.767
Audit records help you trace key calls

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.300
and investigate what went wrong.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.967
The skill marketplace helps you

00:00:39.967 --> 00:00:42.033
find, inspect, and install workflows,

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:44.000
and share reusable skills with your team.

00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:48.067
Larger teams can package naming, checking,

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.467
and export rules as skills,

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.767
sharing consistent workflows across projects.

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:58.300
DCC MCP. Skills and MCP, working together.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:00:59.900
Visit our website

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.233
and start with one reusable creative workflow.
